  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> be a symmetric matrix of order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> with integer entries. If the sum of the diagonal elements of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the possible number of such matrices is:"
  },
